<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Infographic divided into two panels comparing microbial inhibition and promotion of wound healing; left side shows disrupted healing via biofilm, hypoxia, inflammation, and impaired collagen, while right shows enhanced healing with specific microbes, signaling pathways, immune cells, and increased collagen.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating mechanisms by which probiotics support wound healing, organized in quadrants around a central ring labeled Biofilm Disruption, Antibacterial, Oxidative Stress, and Cellular Activity. Diagram includes bacteria, biochemical pathways, skin layers, and molecular interactions showing effects on inflammation, collagen synthesis, biofilm disruption, epithelial migration, angiogenesis, immune modulation, and antibacterial activity using arrows and annotations.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
